# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CONTACT FORM EMAIL — every enquiry is emailed to you through Gmail.
#
# One-time setup (about 5 minutes):
# 1. In the Gmail account that will SEND the emails, turn on 2-Step Verification:
#      Google Account → Security → 2-Step Verification.
# 2. Create an App Password: Google Account → Security → App passwords
#      (or go to myaccount.google.com/apppasswords). Name it "Website".
#      Google shows a 16-letter password — copy it (spaces are fine).
# 3. On your computer: open the file .env.local (same folder as this one; if it
#    doesn't exist, copy this file and rename the copy to .env.local) and fill in
#    the three lines below. Save.
# 4. Test it:  npm run check-email      (add  -- --send  to also send a test email)
# 5. Live site: add the same three names and values in
#      Vercel → your project → Settings → Environment Variables, then redeploy.
#
# Never put the real password in this file or on GitHub — only in .env.local and Vercel.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The Gmail address that sends the emails
SMTP_USER=
# The 16-letter App Password from step 2 (NOT your normal Gmail password)
SMTP_PASS=
# Where enquiries should arrive (leave empty to use SMTP_USER)
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=

# Optional — only change these if you don't use Gmail
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=465
